---
import PageLayout from "../layouts/PageLayout.astro";
import RouteMark from "../components/RouteMark.astro";
import { lenses } from "../lib/studio";
import { site } from "../site.config";
---
<PageLayout title="About" description="Meet Mathius Johnson and the independent practice behind Four Paths.">
  <div class="wrap about-page">
    <header class="about-head"><span class="overline">About / The person behind the work</span><h1>More than<br /><em>one kind of work.</em></h1><p class="lede">Four Paths is the independent studio behind the things I build outside the boundaries of a single job title.</p></header>
    <div class="about-layout"><aside class="side"><RouteMark size={150} /><p class="overline">Mathius Johnson<br />Canada</p></aside><div class="body">
      <p class="opening">I’m Mathius Johnson. I build software, but the questions that bring me to a project often come from somewhere else: practice, family life, games, making things, and wondering how a tool changes the person using it.</p>
      <p>Four Paths gives those inquiries a shared home. It is a product studio, not a consultancy disguised as one. The projects are different because the parts of life they touch are different. What connects them is a preference for specific problems, honest constraints and tools people can put down when the real activity begins.</p>
      <h2>Why four paths?</h2>
      <p>Build, Create, Question and Ground are lenses rather than departments. I use them to notice where a project gets its energy and where it needs to be challenged. An engineering choice may change how much agency someone has. A playful mechanic may make a hard routine easier to begin. A household can expose an assumption that looked perfectly reasonable at a desk.</p>
      <div class="lens-list">{Object.entries(lenses).map(([key, lens]) => <div class={`lens lens-${key}`}><span class="overline">{lens.verb}</span><h3>{lens.name}</h3><p>{lens.description}</p></div>)}</div>
      <h2>How I work</h2>
      <p>I work across product design, mobile interfaces, domain models, APIs and release details. Pillars asks how a screen can support a physical practice without becoming its centre. Chore Credits asks how an app can make a family agreement more visible and fair. Life Atlas asks what progress looks like when a task list is too small a frame.</p>
      <p>The technical work matters. So does changing my mind when a model proves too rigid, a flow asks too much attention, or a better question appears during testing. The <a href="/notes">notes</a> record some of those changes; the <a href="/work">project pages</a> show where they landed.</p>
      <h2>Say hello</h2>
      <p>If a project here connects with something you are making or thinking about, I’d like to hear from you.</p>
      <p><a class="button-link" href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>Email Mathius ↗</a></p>
    </div></div>
  </div>
</PageLayout>
<style>
  .about-page{padding-bottom:4rem}.about-head{padding:4rem 0 5rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line)}.about-head h1{margin:.8rem 0 1rem}.about-head h1 em{font-weight:400;color:var(--ink-soft)}.about-layout{display:grid;grid-template-columns:240px minmax(0,720px);justify-content:space-between;gap:5rem;padding:5rem 0}.side{color:var(--ink-muted)}.side .overline{margin-top:2rem}.body{font-size:1.05rem}.body p{color:var(--ink-soft)}.body .opening{font:400 clamp(1.5rem,2.3vw,2rem)/1.35 var(--display);color:var(--ink);margin-bottom:2rem}.body h2{margin-top:4rem}.lens-list{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;margin:2.5rem 0;border-top:1px solid var(--line)}.lens{padding:1.5rem 1rem 1rem 0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line)}.lens h3{font-size:1.5rem;margin:.35rem 0}.lens p{font-size:.9rem;margin:0}.lens .overline{color:var(--lens-color)}.lens-build{--lens-color:var(--technology)}.lens-create{--lens-color:var(--creativity)}.lens-question{--lens-color:var(--philosophy)}.lens-ground{--lens-color:var(--family)}@media(max-width:700px){.about-layout{grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:2rem;padding:3rem 0}.side{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:2rem}.side .overline{margin:0}.about-head{padding:3rem 0}}@media(max-width:450px){.lens-list{grid-template-columns:1fr}}
</style>
